# Keynection server settings: every name the server, the Dockerfile and the start scripts read, with what it does.
# The server reads the environment directly (Windows: "set NAME=value" before starting; Render: the service's
# Environment tab; Docker: -e NAME=value). Nothing loads this file: it is the reference, kept complete by
# backend/tests/test_env_example.py. Names from before the rename (JIRAN_...) still work.
# A line starting with # is an explanation or an example; remove the # to set that value.

# ---------- Which mode ----------
# 1 (default): the judges' demo. A fictional phase, the cast switcher, the guide, "Reset demo data" and sample
# photos; the server trusts the unit number in each request so judges can switch roles.
# 0: a pilot. Real households sign in with their phone's digital key, nothing fictional, never reset.
KEYNECTION_DEMO_MODE=1

# ---------- The online demo ----------
# Required online in demo mode: the whole site sits behind our three-language password page. Never set in a pilot.
# KEYNECTION_SITE_PASSWORD=change-me
# Demo only: after this many quiet minutes the shared demo rebuilds the fictional phase (default 20). A pilot ignores it.
# KEYNECTION_DEMO_IDLE_MINUTES=20

# ---------- AI (optional: everything works without it) ----------
# Claude, by design: turns on translation of typed words, the calmer wording and the one-sentence renovation notice.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The Claude model (default claude-opus-5-5; claude-haiku-5-5 answers faster).
# KEYNECTION_AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# Gemini's free tier, DEMO ONLY: Google may use what is sent to improve its products, so a pilot ignores it and warns.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# The Gemini model (default gemini-3.8-flash).
# KEYNECTION_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# 0 turns AI off whatever keys are set (a rehearsal of the no-AI path).
# KEYNECTION_AI=1

# ---------- A pilot (KEYNECTION_DEMO_MODE=0) ----------
# The pilot's https:// address. Digital keys are bound to it, so choose it before the first household joins.
# KEYNECTION_ORIGIN=https://keynection.example.com
# First start only: the first estate-office staff member. Their one-time sign-in link appears in the server log.
# KEYNECTION_FIRST_STAFF=Farah Aziz
# The first staff member's role: estate (default) or sdp.
# KEYNECTION_FIRST_STAFF_ROLE=estate
# How push services can contact this server, e.g. a mailto: address (default: the origin).
# KEYNECTION_PUSH_CONTACT=mailto:estate@example.com
# Where the daily backups go (default: a backups folder next to the database); kept 14 days.
# KEYNECTION_BACKUP_DIR=/data/backups
# On an old server only, after a move: sends every visit to the same page at the new address.
# KEYNECTION_MOVED_TO=https://new-address.example.com

# ---------- Where things are (set by the Dockerfile and the scripts; rarely changed by hand) ----------
# The SQLite database; photos, comparison images and backups live next to it (the container uses /data/app.db).
# KEYNECTION_DB_PATH=/data/app.db
# The built web app the server serves on / (default frontend/dist).
# KEYNECTION_STATIC_DIR=
# Extra browser origins allowed to call the API, comma-separated (default: the Vite dev server on port 5173).
# KEYNECTION_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# ---------- The start scripts (start-demo.bat, start-demo.sh, start-dev.bat) ----------
# 1: don't open the browser when the demo starts.
# KEYNECTION_NO_BROWSER=1
# 1: also listen on the local network and print the address phones on the same Wi-Fi can open (same as the --lan
# argument). Rehearsals only, on a trusted network: the local demo has no password.
# KEYNECTION_LAN=1

# ---------- Set by the host ----------
# PORT is set by Render or Railway; the scripts use 8000 locally.
